==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fiu-pro|fi}} {{term/t|fiu-pro|*śuri-||to die}}, which is from Proto-Uralic *śure. It is a cognate with eg. Estonian {{term|surema||to die|lang=et}}. Compare also {{term|surma|lang=fi}}. The modern meaning is by contamination from {{term|surkea|lang=fi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|sur|ra}}
* {{rhymes|lang=fi|urːɑ}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈsurːɑˣ]}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=fi}} To [[mourn]], [[grieve]] (''very often because of sb's death'').
# {{context|transitive|lang=fi}} To [[mourn]], [[grieve]] (over sb = ''[[partitive]]; over a dead person'').

